WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.230 align:start position:0%
 
i  was born in 1872  my parents died when i was still in  infant  and so i was brought up by my  grandparents  can you tell us something about your  grandfather  yes i could tell you something about my  grandfather  he was born  in the early years of the french  revolution  he was a member of parliament while  napoleon was still on the throne  [Music]  in common with all the  greek followers of fox  he thought english hostility to napoleon  was excessive  [Music]  it was he who introduced the reform bill  in 1832 which started england on the  road towards  democracy he was prime minister during  your mexican war  during the revolutions of 1848  i remember him quite well  but as you can see he belonged to an age  that now seems rather removed  and  [Music]  in the world where i was young  was a solid world  a world where all kinds of things that  have now disappeared were thought to be  going to last forever didn't dawn on  people's things  see  english people certainly regarded  english naval supremacy as a sort of law  of nature britannia ruled the waves it  indeed occurred to us that that might  stop  everything even with bismarck  bismarck misregarded his  rascal  and  we thought i was a sort of uneducated  farmer  but it was assumed that the influence of  gertie and schindler would gradually  bring germany back to a more civilized  point of view  and moreover  we thought of germany as only a land  power germany had at that time known  navy  we weren't all afraid of germany in fact  liberal opinion was more favorable to  germany than to france at that time  the german bismarck himself  compared germany and england to an  elephant and a whale each formidable in  its own element but no danger to each  other  and that was how we felt so we were not  afraid of bismarck at all  it was thought that there was going to  be ordered progress throughout the world  gradually every country was going to  take departments there was going to be  a bicameral legislature and two parties  and it will all go to be exactly like  everywhere all over the world  my grandmother used to laugh because one  time she said to the russian ambassador  perhaps someday you will have a  parliament in russia only god forbid my  dear lady russell  except for the first word the russian  ambassador at the present day might give  the same answer  but  that was the assumption it was all going  to be orderly all quite nice  the  atmosphere  apart from politics there was one of  puritan piety  very great party very great austerity  we always had family prayers at eight  and before family prayers i had to do  half an hour's practice at the piano  which i hated  although there were eight servants in  the house  the food was always the utmost  simplicity  and  even if what there was if there was  anything at all nice i wasn't allowed to  have it because it wasn't good for  children to eat nice things  for instance there would be rice pudding  and apple tart  don't upset the apricot and i had the  rice pudding  and there was extreme austerity in all  those ways  my grandmother until she was over 70  would never sit in an armchair until  after dinner  ever  [Music]

